      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I did the opposite, making an avatar larger. I get a similar issue, where my viewball drifts below my head as I remeasure to a larger version of my avatar, so it seems to be the opposite of what happens compared to remeasuring to a smaller avatar. This only happens in FBT for me. It seems to work fine in 3 point. My feet also seem to drift up into the air as well.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-07-16T03:33:07.562Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I constructed an avatar with a resize feature by:\n1. Creating an animation which scales the avatar root (starting at scale 1 at time 0 and going to 0.25 at the end of the animation)\n2. Adding a layer to the FX controller, with weight 1, in additive mode, with the above animation as the only and initial state, and with the normalized time connected to a \"Scale\" parameter\n3. Adding a second FX layer which would repeatedly call Remeasure Avatar while \n\"ScaleMenuOpen\" is 1, then invoke one more time when it transitions to 0\n4. Set up a radial puppet to set ScaleMenuOpen when open and to control Scale with the analog value.\nThis largely works, but in FBT it seems the calibration drifts very slightly. In this video I'm holding my hand still over the headset, but you can see it drifting as I shrink and returning to its original position when I return to my original size: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dWCC72JJaJ8\nIf you look closely, you can see my knees bent slightly in the smaller state as well.",
